{"id":"20260826T001908.182813463Z-e5bb1889","time":"2026-08-26T00:19:08.182813463Z","session_id":"session-20260826T001249.419106478Z","task_id":"task-1787703169419346745","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  There is no way to ask why a specific piece of governing knowledge exists.\n\nAdd to internal/architect the exported function:\n\n    func RunWhy(caller Caller, domain, id string) (string, error)\n\nGiven an id it resolves the rule through the supplied Caller's awareness_resolve tool and returns a report carrying what the graph holds about it. An empty id is an error naming the expected form. The class is not assumed from the id: an architect copies whatever they were shown, so a rule held under another kind must still be found rather than refused on a guess, and an id carrying a class prefix must resolve to the same rule as the bare one, with no prefix sent to Sensei. The domain scopes the query when non-empty and is omitted when empty. An id the graph holds nothing under is an error naming that id.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] internal/architect/run.go defines Caller.CallTool and existing architect commands conditionally include domain only when it is non-empty. (internal/architect/run.go:Caller and existing MCP-backed commands) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei's documented C4 contract makes awareness_resolve an available structured architect-context surface, while repository rules prohibit locally re-deriving Sensei-owned state. (docs/contracts.md:C4 and rules R3-R4) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The scoped preflight examined both planned files, classified the change LOW_RISK with local blast radius and no approval gate, and reported that no anchored rule applies. (internal/architect/run.go and internal/architect/run_test.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei resolves invariant:sensei_code.retrieval.selection_routes_a_query_and_never_creates_a_claim as active and high severity; it requires bounded retrieval and explicit empty answers rather than widening. (RunWhy lookup and not-found behavior) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] The authored invariant sensei_code.evidence.counts_carry_their_provenance protects internal/architect/ and requires reports not to turn absent or bounded evidence into stronger claims. (internal/architect/) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The current checkout has no internal/architect/run_test.go, while Sensei's indexed code context associates RunWhy with internal/architect/run.go and identifies focused RunWhy test symbols in internal/architect/run_test.go. (planned implementation and test placement) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] The existing TUI dispatches architect package functions explicitly and currently has no RunWhy route. (internal/tui/model.go:Model.senseiCommand) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] task_briefing returned exactly: tool call error: tool call failed for `sensei/task_briefing`; Caused by: Mcp error: -32000: no task session exists in this repository. (task-aware briefing for internal/architect/run.go) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: bounded-knowledge-gap\n"}
